.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SRP_USER_PWD_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SRP_user_pwd_new ,
.Nm SRP_user_pwd_free ,
.Nm SRP_user_pwd_set1_ids ,
.Nm SRP_user_pwd_set_gN ,
.Nm SRP_user_pwd_set0_sv
.Nd Functions to create a record of SRP user verifier information
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/srp.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft SRP_user_pwd *
.Fo SRP_user_pwd_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SRP_user_pwd_free
.Fa "SRP_user_pwd *user_pwd"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SRP_user_pwd_set1_ids
.Fa "SRP_user_pwd *user_pwd"
.Fa "const char *id"
.Fa "const char *info"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SRP_user_pwd_set_gN
.Fa "SRP_user_pwd *user_pwd"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *g"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *N"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SRP_user_pwd_set0_sv
.Fa "SRP_user_pwd *user_pwd"
.Fa "BIGNUM *s"
.Fa "BIGNUM *v"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
There are no available replacement functions at this time.
.Pp
The
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_new
function allocates a structure to store a user verifier record.
.Pp
The
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_free
function frees up the
.Fa user_pwd
structure.
If
.Fa user_pwd
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
The
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_set1_ids
function sets the username to
.Fa id
and the optional user info to
.Fa info
for
.Fa user_pwd .
The library allocates new copies of
.Fa id
and
.Fa info ,
the caller still owns the original memory.
.Pp
The
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_set0_sv
function sets the user salt to
.Fa s
and the verifier to
.Fa v
for
.Fa user_pwd .
The library takes ownership of the values, they should not be freed by
the caller.
.Pp
The
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_set_gN
function sets the SRP group parameters for
.Fa user_pwd .
The memory is not freed by
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_free ,
the caller must make sure it is freed once it is no longer used.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_set1_ids
returns 1 on success and 0 on failure or if
.Fa id
was NULL.
.Pp
.Fn SRP_user_pwd_set0_sv
returns 1 if both
.Fa s
and
.Fa v
are not NULL, 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl-srp 1 ,
.Xr SRP_create_verifier 3 ,
.Xr SRP_VBASE_new 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_srp_password 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were made public in OpenSSL 3.0 and are deprecated.
